<script>
	import Next from "$lib/components/next.svelte";
  import asciiAvif from "$lib/assets/visual/ascii.avif"
  import asciiGif from "$lib/assets/visual/ascii.gif"
  import boxDrawAvif from "$lib/assets/visual/box-draw.avif"
  import boxDrawGif from "$lib/assets/visual/box-draw.gif"
</script>

# visual

press `v` to toggle between ascii and box-draw rendering. the selected style applies to the keyboard in default mode and the keys shown in keycast mode.

ditto uses your terminal palette so it fits your existing color scheme.

## ascii

<picture>
  <source srcset={asciiAvif} type="image/avif">
  <img src={asciiGif} alt="ASCII visual" width="826" height="332" fetchpriority="high"/>
</picture>

if you prefer a traditional, more disconnected look, then use the ascii visual.

## box-draw 

<picture>
  <source srcset={boxDrawAvif} type="image/avif">
  <img src={boxDrawGif} alt="Box draw visual" width="826" height="332" fetchpriority="high"/>
</picture>

if you prefer a smoother look, then use the box-draw visual which uses box drawing characters.

